%I A401603 #15 Nov 06 2026 10:39:10
%S A401603 0,1,3,5,10,24,49,231
%N A401603 Maximum number of instructions executed before executing the halting instruction at the end of a halting computation of an n-instruction register Minsky machine.
%C A401603 We start with initially empty registers and include exactly one Halt instruction.
%H A401603 bbchallenge, <a href="https://wiki.bbchallenge.org/wiki/Register_machine">Register machine</a>
%H A401603 Tibor Rado, <a href="https://gwern.net/doc/cs/computable/1962-rado.pdf">On Non-Computable Functions</a>, Bell System Technical Journal, Vol. 41 (May 1962), #3, 877-884.
%e A401603 A program for a(5)=10 is:
%e A401603   1: A+ -> 2
%e A401603   2: B+ -> 3
%e A401603   3: A- -> 2, 4
%e A401603   4: B- -> 3, 5
%e A401603   5: HALT
%Y A401603 Cf. A081419.
%K A401603 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A401603 1,3
%A A401603 _Zhuorui He_, Oct 30 2026
